# Optimization-First Architecture (Default Design Bar)

Every **new** RDE domain, experiment hot path, evaluator, or campaign feature
must be designed for performance **from the first commit**, not as a later pass.

Before marking work done, verify:

1. **Machine profile** — run `.venv/bin/python3 -m rde machine-profile` and pick
   backends accordingly (`mlx`/`auto` on `apple_silicon_mac`, `numpy` on
   `intel_mac`).
2. **GPU / MLX** — hot loops run batched on MLX when Metal is available; no
   per-step NumPy roundtrips; cache device tensors.
3. **Vectorization** — no Python loops over \(2^N\), rows, candidates, or state
   dimensions unless documented as an intentional small-\(N\) setup exception.
4. **Batching** — group compatible instances so `prepare_instances_batch` and
   pipeline batch_size can reuse work.
5. **Workers** — CPU-bound orchestration uses `workers > 1` where process pools
   are safe; parent pre-batches GPU work before worker dispatch when applicable.
6. **Parity tests** — every fast path has a reference or harness check; record
   requested vs effective backend in manifests when fallback occurs.

If a prototype is intentionally scalar, label it `theoretical-only` or keep it
off the campaign path until the optimized contract exists.

See `docs/engineering/agent-correction-playbook.md` and
`.cursor/rules/rde-performance-guardrails.mdc`.
